# netsurf: inline <svg> with an auto dimension is sized like browsers do (patch 217)
# Generated 2026-10-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser 92dfbf1 (patch stack through 216)
#
# An inline <svg> is a replaced box (fixes202: SVG_INLINE | REPLACE_DIM)
# with no object, so layout had no intrinsic size or ratio for it: a
# width or height left auto came out 0 (line layout's "unknown replaced
# size" branch), and in a flex row the block path made it square. Icons
# sized by one dimension -- <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="w-6">, or a
# width attribute alone -- and responsive illustrations with only a
# viewBox disappeared.
#
# vb_inline_svg_resolve_size() (vb_inline_svg.c) reads the root's viewBox
# from the DOM and resolves CSS 2.1 10.3.2 / 10.6.2 with SVG's intrinsic
# ratio: one given dimension gives the other through the ratio; neither
# given, with a viewBox, is the containing block's width (0 for the
# min/max-width pass); without a viewBox the default object size, 300 x
# 150. layout_line's inline-replaced sizing uses it (then min/max-width
# and -height clamp), the min/max-width pass uses it for an auto width,
# and the block-level REPLACE_DIM path uses it instead of a square.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/CSS-svg-size.html (SVGSIZE217, 5 checks,
# Chromium 5/5; the auto dimension was 0 before, failing 1-4): width
# given, height given, neither (container width), no viewBox (300 x 150),
# both attributes unchanged.
